          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जागणो — jāgṇo — \"to wake up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हूं रोज तड़कै जागूं हूं। hū̃ roj taṛkai jāgū̃ hū̃. I wake up at daybreak every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): हूं आज तड़कै जाग्यो, hū̃ āj taṛkai jāgyo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जागणो (jāgṇo) is inherited from Sanskrit jāgrati, \"they are awake\"; CDIAL lists Marwari jāgṇo, \"to wake\", under it (CDIAL 5175). Its partner जगावणो, to wake someone, is already yours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
