              "text": "खंगाळणो (khaṅgāḷṇo) comes from a reconstructed khakkhālayati, \"rinses\", which CDIAL thinks imitates the sound of rinsing; it lists Hindi khãgālnā and a Gujarati verb for rinsing the mouth in the morning (CDIAL 3762). CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry."
